1 FAMC @F03@
1 FAMS @F01@
1 NOTE Born **Patrick Brunty**, the eldest of ten children of a County Down farm labourer. He opened a school at sixteen, and in 1802 travelled to St John's College, Cambridge, where he entered his name in
2 CONC  the new spelling he kept for the rest of his life.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ordained in 1806, he served curacies in Essex, Shropshire and the West Riding before being appointed perpetual curate of Haworth in 1820. He held the living for forty-one years.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was in print long before any of his children were, with *Cottage Poems* (1811) and *The Rural Minstrel* (1813). In 1846 Charlotte took him to Manchester for cataract surgery, and began *Jane Eyre*
2 CONC  in the lodgings while he recovered.
2 CONT
2 CONT He outlived his wife and all six of their children.
2 CONT
2 CONT More about the family at [the Brontë Parsonage Museum](https://www.bronte.org.uk/).
