0 @I11@ INDI
1 NAME Patrick Branwell /Brontë/
2 GIVN Patrick Branwell
2 SURN Brontë
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 26 JUN 1817
2 PLAC Thornton, Yorkshire
1 DEAT
2 DATE 24 SEP 1848
2 PLAC Haworth, Yorkshire
1 FAMC @F01@
1 NOTE The only son, and the one everything was expected of. He trained as a portrait painter, kept a studio in Bradford, and worked in turn as a tutor and as a railway clerk at Luddenden Foot, where he was
2 CONC  dismissed over the accounts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Around 1834 he painted his three sisters together, then painted himself out of the group and left a pillar where he had stood. It is the only surviving group portrait of them, and it hangs in the
2 CONC  National Portrait Gallery.
2 CONT
2 CONT He wrote too, publishing verse in the *Halifax Guardian* — before any of his sisters were in print. Dismissed from his last post at Thorp Green in 1845, he spent three years in debt, opium and drink,
2 CONC  and died in September 1848, aged thirty-one.
1 OBJE
2 FORM jpeg
2 TITL Patrick Branwell Brontë, painted by John Brown. Brontë Parsonage Museum. Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons.
