0 @I12@ INDI
1 NAME Emily Jane /Brontë/
2 GIVN Emily Jane
2 SURN Brontë
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 30 JUL 1818
2 PLAC Thornton, Yorkshire
1 DEAT
2 DATE 19 DEC 1848
2 PLAC Haworth, Yorkshire
1 FAMC @F01@
1 NOTE The most private of the three, and the one who most disliked being away from Haworth. She lasted three months at Roe Head and less than a year in Brussels. At home she kept the household running,
2 CONC  walked the moors, and wrote — with Anne — the long Gondal saga the two of them never stopped adding to.
2 CONT
2 CONT > 1801 — I have just returned from a visit to my landlord.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Wuthering Heights* appeared in 1847 and baffled its reviewers, who took its violence for coarseness and its author for a man. It is now the more read of the two 1847 novels.
2 CONT
2 CONT She caught cold at Branwell's funeral in September 1848, refused every doctor offered her, and died three months later.
