0 @I13@ INDI
1 NAME Anne /Brontë/
2 GIVN Anne
2 SURN Brontë
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 17 JAN 1820
2 PLAC Thornton, Yorkshire
1 DEAT
2 DATE 28 MAY 1849
2 PLAC Scarborough, Yorkshire
1 FAMC @F01@
1 NOTE The youngest, and the only one of the sisters who held a post outside the family for any length of time: five years as a governess, mostly at Thorp Green, which gave her both her novels their
2 CONC  material.
2 CONT
2 CONT - *Agnes Grey* (1847) — a governess's life, written flat and without consolation
2 CONT - *The Tenant of Wildfell Hall* (1848) — a woman leaves an alcoholic husband and earns her own living
2 CONT
2 CONT The second sold fast and was attacked for its subject. After Anne's death Charlotte declined to have it reprinted, calling the choice of subject a mistake, and it stayed hard to find for decades.
2 CONT
2 CONT She died at Scarborough in May 1849, seven months after Emily, and is the only one of the family not buried at Haworth.
1 OBJE
2 FORM jpeg
2 TITL Anne Brontë, painted by her brother Branwell, c. 1834. Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons.
